.TH NRSC5\-STUDIO 1 "May 2026" "nrsc5-studio 0.3.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nrsc5\-studio \- graphical HD Radio receiver built on nrsc5 and SoapySDR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nrsc5\-studio
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B NRSC5 Studio
is a native desktop application for listening to HD Radio FM broadcasts
(87.5\(en108 MHz) with an RTL\-SDR, SDRplay, or HackRF One software\-defined
radio. It is built around the open\-source
.BR nrsc5 (1)
HD Radio demodulator and the SoapySDR device layer, and provides a
graphical interface with tuner controls, a SIS\-aware subchannel selector,
album\-art collage, 24\-hour song log, live spectrum / waterfall / QPSK
constellation scopes, closed\-loop AGC, TPEG traffic decoding, and
weather\-radar animation.
.PP
The application takes no command\-line arguments. Settings are persisted
between runs in standard XDG locations (see
.BR FILES ).
.SH PREREQUISITES
NRSC5 Studio requires the
.BR nrsc5 (1)
helper binary to be installed and available on
.BR PATH .
The
.B nrsc5
helper is not packaged in Debian or Ubuntu and must be built from source.
A convenience installer is shipped at
.IR /usr/share/nrsc5\-studio/install\-nrsc5\-helper.sh ;
run it once as a regular user to clone, build, and install
.B nrsc5
into
.IR /usr/local/bin .
Source code and full build instructions are available at
.UR https://github.com/theori\-io/nrsc5
.UE .
.PP
SoapySDR and at least one SoapySDR module package (for example
.IR soapysdr\-module\-rtlsdr )
must also be installed so the application can talk to your SDR
hardware.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nrsc5\-studio/config.toml
User\-level configuration: last frequency, presets, gain mode, AGC
state, theme, SDR driver settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nrsc5\-studio/
Persistent data: album\-art cache, play log, dock layout, SDR
diagnostics snapshot.
